     "speaker": "meera",
     "tone": "explainer",
     "text": "Your two eyes look from different but similar directions, so they see different images.",
     "kind": "fact",
     "claims": [
      "c_f1"
     ]
    },
    {
     "speaker": "arjun",
     "tone": "curious",
     "text": "And with an eye shut, I lose the other image?",
     "kind": "question",
     "act": {
      "expr": "curious"
     }
    },
    {
     "speaker": "meera",
     "tone": "explainer",
     "text": "Right. Your brain combines the two images, and you see a single 3D view with depth.",
     "kind": "fact",
     "claims": [
      "c_f2"
     ]
    }
